From e0542234d04feca9ef93fe0a08fd368348fbbdd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:20:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [buildsteps] Clear the binary add-on result markers on every
 build

The add-on build appends to cmake/addons/.success and .failure, and only
an add-on build clears them. A build with BUILD_BINARY_ADDONS off skips
that, so it inherits the markers of the last add-on build in the same
Jenkins workspace and the post-build check reports add-on failures for a
build that built none. Seen on a LINUX-ARM-GLES PR build after a master
build lost its agent mid add-on build.

Clear them with the build failed file, as make-addons.bat already does
on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7381d55b31415b5071dcc51ac9f75be58587cc21)
(cherry picked from commit 628367ff7dbfa91d6870874494d3d15484d235b2)
